{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cf1Gzb7Yux8zVaFVrM1PF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MpLSCfGUUyocjzhtDexQHc","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Write updated Kotlin files with confirm endpoint","prompt":"I need you to write/update three Kotlin files in the sample-service project. Here are the exact requirements:\n\n1. **ShipmentController.kt** at `/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-8038176a-7ec2-441f-b46c-09ab88a1aec0/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentController.kt`\n\nAdd a new confirm endpoint with this signature and behavior:\n```kotlin\n@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")\nfun confirm(@PathVariable shipmentId: String): Shipment\n```\n\nThe endpoint should:\n- Throw ResourceNotFoundException (404) with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND if shipment not found\n- Throw ConflictException (409) with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS if status is CANCELLED\n- Return shipment unchanged if it's already CONFIRMED (idempotent)\n- Save and return the shipment with status changed to CONFIRMED if it's CREATED\n\n2. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** at `/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-8038176a-7ec2-441f-b46c-09ab88a1aec0/sample-service/src/test/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentControllerTest.kt`\n\nAdd four new test methods:\n- `confirming a CREATED shipment moves it to CONFIRMED`: POST to /shipments/{id}/confirm on CREATED shipment, verify status becomes CONFIRMED\n- `confirming an already CONFIRMED shipment succeeds (idempotent)`: Create, confirm, then confirm again, verify still CONFIRMED and 200 status\n- `confirming a CANCELLED shipment returns 409 with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS`: Manually set status to CANCELLED via repository, POST to confirm endpoint, verify 409 status and error code\n- `confirming a non-existent shipment returns 404`: POST to confirm endpoint with non-existent ID, verify 404 status and SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND code\n\nNote: ShipmentStatus enum has CREATED, CONFIRMED, and CANCELLED values. The Shipment data class is immutable, so use .copy() to create modified versions.\n\nUse the existing file contents I read earlier as the base. Follow the exact code style and patterns already in these files.","run_in_background":false},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":218,"cache_read_input_tokens":15800,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":218,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01JRD2GbQmgfE62BYnkVG74F","session_id":"ae3a7f7c-e754-4932-9459-9b57e85ab55a","uuid":"34992ac1-93e8-4845-b2ae-721f94528b39","timestamp":"2026-09-13T10:25:19.463Z","request_id":"req_011Cf1GzaYKWQ6SyJBebxhkt","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Update shipment endpoint files with confirm functionality"}
